    "angles": "1. Lead on this: a Ferrari-built V8, naturally aspirated, 454 horsepower - and these now go for around 2,000. It was a six-figure car new. That makes it the cheapest way to own an engine Ferrari assembled, and it comes from before everything went turbo.\n2. Cover the catch, because it is what owners actually talk about: the interior coating goes sticky. The soft-touch finish on the buttons and switches degrades with age and heat, and owners of these treat it as inevitable rather than unlucky - there is a cottage industry stripping and refinishing the switchgear. Say it as the complaint that follows the car, which is what it is.\n3. For the head-to-head use the naturally aspirated Ferrari California - 453 horsepower against this car's 454, and the Ferrari costs several times as much for the same power.",
