  "script": "Ferrari assembled this naturally aspirated V8, and it'll rev to 7,200 rpm without a single turbo. The 2015 Maserati GranTurismo Sport used a naturally aspirated 4.7-liter V8 producing 454 horsepower. Pininfarina designed the body, while this car's MC Sport Line package adds stiffer springs, dampers and anti-roll bars. That trident's modeled after the one on Bologna's Fountain of Neptune. Its six-speed ZF torque-converter automatic came from the Quattroporte Sport GT S and drives the rear wheels through a limited-slip differential. Ferrari built the 4.7-liter V8 in Maranello with wet-sump lubrication and diamond-like coatings on its camshaft lobes and tappets, and it produces 384 pound-feet of torque. The cabin's notorious soft-touch buttons turn sticky as their coating deteriorates with age and heat; specialists strip and refinish them. It's a familiar complaint. They cost about $130,000 new before options, but they go for about $31,000 today. Would you take that gamble?",
